        "source_url": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/43978818",
        "coordinate_status": "OSM mapped feature representative point; not a navigation entrance",
        "art_english": "The Long Corridor of the Summer Palace: an exceptionally long covered wooden lakeside gallery receding in perspective, repeated vermilion columns, intricate teal blue green painted beams and rafters, a gently undulating gray tiled roof with occasional small pavilion sections. Kunming Lake on one side and golden trees on the other. Clearly a linear open covered passage, not a bridge or wall. No readable painted text.",
        "minutes": 40,
        "walk_after": 15,
        "detail": "彩绘长廊 · 临湖秋色",
        "time": "10:55"
