        "lon": 116.2679821,
        "lat": 39.9978268,
        "osm": "way/43977851",
        "source_url": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/43977851",
        "coordinate_status": "OSM mapped feature representative point; not a navigation entrance",
        "art_english": "Tower of Buddhist Incense, Foxiangge, on Longevity Hill: the unmistakable tall OCTAGONAL three-storey pavilion with FOUR projecting yellow glazed eave layers, green-blue painted timber details, red columns, on a massive high square stone terrace reached by long steep symmetrical stairs. Lower palace roofs nestle below and forest crowns the hill. Different from Jingshan Wanchun Pavilion: tall octagonal body with four eave layers, not square three-tier roof.",
        "minutes": 75,
        "walk_after": 20,
        "detail": "八角佛阁 · 登高望湖",
        "time": "11:50"
      },
      {
        "name": "清晏舫",
        "lon": 116.2636803,
